-- title:
--   Preimage of the origin section in the origin chart
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, and $G$ a relative group law on the structure morphism $\mathrm{Proj}$ of the graded quotient ring of the projective Weierstrass model of $W$ over $\operatorname{Spec} T$, i.e. a `RelativeGroupLaw` on `projModelStrCR W`: a functorial multiplication, unit and inverse on the sets of $T$-morphisms $T' \to \mathrm{Proj}$ over the base, subject to the group axioms and naturality of multiplication. Assume that the unit section $G.\mathrm{one}(\mathbf{1})$ lies in the origin chart in the strong sense that there is a ring homomorphism $\chi_0 \colon \mathcal{O}(W) \to T$, where $\mathcal{O}(W) =$ `OriginChartRing W` is the degree-zero homogeneous localisation of the projective model ring at the coordinate $Y$, such that the underlying morphism of that unit section equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\chi_0)$ followed by the chart immersion `originChartι W`, and such that $\chi_0$ kills the two chart coordinates $X/Y$ and $Z/Y$ (`xOverY W` and `zOverY W`). Then for every commutative ring $B$ and every ring homomorphism $\chi \colon \mathcal{O}(W) \to B$, the pullback along $\operatorname{Spec}(\chi)$ followed by `originChartι W` of the kernel ideal sheaf `Scheme.Hom.ker` of the unit section, evaluated on the affine open $\top$ of $\operatorname{Spec} B$ and transported to $B$ through $\Gamma\mathrm{Spec}$, is the ideal of $B$ generated by $\chi(X/Y)$ and $\chi(Z/Y)$.
--
--   This identifies the ideal cutting out the locus where a $B$-point of the origin chart coincides with the zero section: it is generated by the images of the two affine chart coordinates. It is used in the computation of the ideal of the $n$-torsion subscheme in the origin chart, [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.map_ideal_comap_torsionIdeal_eq_span_nthSeries`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.map_ideal_comap_torsionIdeal_eq_span_nthSeries).
